<section>
  <p class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "guides", label_type: :nav, class: "cta" %></p>
  <h1>Switch on Go and find its controls.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Press the button to switch skyBlip Go on. Hold it for two seconds to switch it off. The touch-sensitive pad moves through pages and silences alarms.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">In your hand</h2>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="controls">Find the pad, <span class="highlight">then the button</span>.</h3>
      <p>The pad is touch-sensitive, on the top edge. On the left side, the button is the lower of the two controls. RESET is above it. The USB-C port is on the right. Two lights sit beside the screen: skyBlip's red, green or blue light and the charger's red light.</p>
      <p>The e-paper screen keeps its image without power. The logo means the Go is off.</p>
    </div>
    <%= render "shared/device", device: :go, label: "skyBlip Go with its pad, button, RESET, lights and USB-C port marked", marks: { pad: t("devices.pad"), button: t("devices.button"), reset: t("devices.reset"), lights: t("devices.lights"), usb: t("devices.usb") } %>
  </div>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Gesture</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Tap the pad</th><td>Opens the next page. On a request, refuses it: the screen's CANCEL key.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Touch the pad, 1&nbsp;s</th><td>Silences an active alarm. With no alarm, returns to the radar.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Press the button</th><td>If Go is off, switches it on at the radar page. On a page, opens its menu. In a menu, changes the selected value. On a request, accepts it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Hold the button, 2&nbsp;s</th><td>Switches off. The logo stays on the screen.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>The same hold, finger on the pad</th><td>Switches off with a blank screen, for storage. An image left all winter leaves a shadow.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Hold the button and plug the charger in</th><td>Starts and charges. Plugging in alone charges and leaves it off.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Press RESET</th><td>Restarts the Go.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Press RESET twice within half a second</th><td>Opens TECHOBOOT, a USB drive for installing skyBlip. Briefing asks for this only if it cannot restart the Go itself.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="light">Read the colour <span class="highlight">and the rhythm</span>.</h3>
      <p>The skyBlip light flashes to save the battery. Your position is known when the satellite receiver knows where you are.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Light</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span> Green, every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>Running, with a position.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--blue" aria-hidden="true"></span> Blue, every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>Running, no position yet.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--blue" aria-hidden="true"></span> Two winks every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>A diagnostic recording started from Briefing is running. The colour still shows the position state.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red, fast flicker</th><td>A traffic alarm is active.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red, every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>Battery low.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red, every 600&nbsp;ms</th><td>Battery critical. Land and charge.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span> One green pulse, 400&nbsp;ms</th><td>Just switched on. On skyBlip Go+, you feel it too.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Three short red pulses</th><td>Switching off. On the Go+, you feel these too.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Dark</th><td>Off.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>The charger's separate red light stays lit while charging and goes out when the battery is full. It blinks if the battery is missing or faulty.</p>
</section>

<section id="type" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Choose your aircraft type</h2>
  <p>Choose an aircraft type and callsign during installation, or set them later. In <%= link_to "Briefing", briefing_root_path %>, open your Go's page. On Go, press the button from the radar and open the <code>AIRCRAFT</code> menu. <code>TYPE</code> sets the aircraft type. <code>CALLSIGN</code> sets <%= link_to_page "controls", label: "your callsign", anchor: "callsign" %>.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="compare">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Name in Briefing</th><th scope="col">Name on Go</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Light aircraft</th><td><code>LIGHT</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Heavy aircraft</th><td><code>HEAVY</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Light helicopter</th><td><code>LIGHT HELI</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Heavy helicopter</th><td><code>HEAVY HELI</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Glider</th><td><code>GLIDER</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Balloon</th><td><code>BALLOON</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Microlight</th><td><code>MICROLIGHT</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Paraglider</th><td><code>PARAGLIDER</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Skydiver</th><td><code>SKYDIVER</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">VTOL</th><td><code>VTOL</code></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Gyroplane</th><td><code>GYROCOPTER</code></td></tr>
